+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# Client meetings — Google Calendar and Meet links.
+# Meetings work without this: hosts then paste a meeting link themselves.
+#   oauth            each person clicks "Connect Google Calendar" once. Works
+#                    with personal Gmail and Workspace accounts. Uses the
+#                    GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID/SECRET above; add
+#                    <CLIENT_ORIGIN>/api/meetings/google/callback as an
+#                    authorized redirect URI on that OAuth client. Outside
+#                    (non-Workspace) accounts need the consent screen published
+#                    and verified for the calendar scopes, or Google expires
+#                    connections after 7 days.
+#   service-account  Google Workspace: an admin authorizes the service account
+#                    above for domain-wide delegation with the scopes
+#                    https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events and
+#                    https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.freebusy, and
+#                    nobody connects anything. Everyone's TapCRM email must be
+#                    their Workspace address.
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# MEETINGS_GOOGLE_AUTH=off
+# 32 random bytes (hex or base64) that seal the stored Google tokens, e.g.
+# `openssl rand -hex 32`. Required for oauth.
+# MEETINGS_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
+
